# Generated by tools/make_helper_proxies.py.
#
# THE ALPHA THIS FILE USED TO ASK FOR. It read: "What they DO
# need and do not have is alpha, which is what would let
# individual hairs read against the eye white instead of a solid
# strip." Both halves exist now.
#
# The half that was missing was NOT the texture. The mesh already
# carried 250 uvs -- and they were a sliver of the BODY atlas,
# u 0.658..0.758 and v 0.927..0.985, inherited from the base mesh.
# A strand sheet sampled through a window that narrow is 0%
# opaque with a mean alpha of 8, so a first attempt at this
# pointed a material at one and made the lashes FAINTER and
# nothing else. `strand_uvs` authors uvs that run along the lash
# instead; see `strand_uvs()` in the generator.
#
# `transparent True` is load-bearing: without the flag the
# renderer discards the alpha and paints the solid strip this
# replaces, which is the trap the eye material records for its
# cornea disc.
name Eyelashes
tag MakeHuman™
ambientColor 0.02 0.02 0.02
diffuseColor 0.12 0.11 0.10
specularColor 0.3 0.3 0.3
shininess 0.2
opacity 1.0
transparent True
diffuseTexture ../lash_strands.png
backfaceCull True
castShadows True
receiveShadows True
shader data/shaders/glsl/litsphere
